{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 39, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Whirlwind Trip to Japan**\n\nLast month, I finally crossed Japan off my bucket list, and what an adventure it was! From the neon-lit streets of Tokyo to the serene bamboo forests of Kyoto, every moment felt like stepping into a different world.\n\nTokyo dazzled with its mix of futuristic skyscrapers and traditional izakayas. I lost count of how many sushi plates I devoured at Tsukiji Market, and the Shibuya Crossing lived up to its reputation—chaotic yet mesmerizing. A day trip to Nikko’s stunning shrines and waterfalls offered a peaceful escape, while the deer in Nara happily nibbled from my hand like old friends.\n\nKyoto’s historic charm stole my heart. Wandering through Fushimi Inari’s endless torii gates, I felt like I’d stumbled into a Studio Ghibli film. The golden Kinkaku-ji Temple glinted under the autumn sun, and the quiet beauty of Arashiyama’s bamboo grove was nothing short of magical.\n\nNo trip to Japan is complete without indulging in its culinary delights. Miso ramen in a tiny Sapporo shop warmed my soul, and matcha everything in Kyoto (especially the lattes!) was a dream. Even the convenience store onigiri tasted like a gourmet meal after a long day of exploring.\n\nJapan’s blend of ancient traditions and cutting-edge innovation left me in awe. The kindness of strangers, the cleanliness of the streets, and the attention to detail in everything from tea ceremonies to bullet trains made it unforgettable.\n\nI left with a camera full of memories and a suitcase full of souvenirs—and already planning my next visit. Because once you go to Japan, one trip is never enough.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.13113585114479065}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.06962104886770248}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.6947354674339294}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -2.7417760065873154e-05}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token"